module generic_call.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: the call passes two arguments to a callable that declares
// one. The refusal names THAT, at the call's own name -- not "generics are not
// supported", which was the honest answer only until 2026-08-21.
//
// The refusal is about the VALUE arity on purpose. The neighbouring shapes --
// an unknown type argument (`dbl[Zork](21)`) and one too many of them
// (`dbl[int, f64](21)`) -- are refused by novac and ACCEPTED by the oracle's
// `check`: it never validates the contents of the turbofish (measured
// 2026-08-21, registered in docs/dev/novac-divergences.md, class O-1c). As a
// fixture either of them would assert a divergence instead of an agreement.
fn dbl[T](x T) -> T => x + x

fn main() {
    println(dbl[int](1, 2))
}
